The simplest way: call `void` on each to suppress the unused-variable error without changing build flags:

```ts
void _showNodeLabels;
void _showSymbolLabels;
void _showSignsInDispositorChains;
```

Alternatively, you could use `useSettingsStore` without destructuring — just call it for the subscription side effect:

```ts
useSettingsStore(s => s.showNodeLabels);
useSettingsStore(s => s.showSymbolLabels);
useSettingsStore(s => s.showSignsInDispositorChains);
```

No assignment at all, so nothing is "unused." This is probably the cleanest option since the comment already explains these are pure render dependencies.

