Store the config object directly instead of unpacking it into fields.

```ts
class HouseCuspPositions {
	private readonly _config: Readonly<HouseCuspPositionsConstructorArgs>;

	constructor(config: HouseCuspPositionsConstructorArgs) {
		this._config = config;
	}

	private copyWith(updates: Partial<HouseCuspPositionsConstructorArgs>): HouseCuspPositions {
		return new HouseCuspPositions({ ...this._config, ...updates });
	}
	// ...
}
```

The interface stays (you need it once), but the field declarations and the field-by-field constructor assignments both disappear. `copyWith` becomes a one-liner. The trade-off is `this._config.date` instead of `this._date` throughout the class.

